WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Sunrise on an empty beach.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.710
A woman walks onto the sand with her dog:

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.460
"I started early, took my dog," Mermaids
come up from the basement to stare at

4
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.300
her.

5
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.820
Then the tide starts to rise.

6
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.130
Past her shoe.

7
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.370
Past her apron and her belt.

8
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.910
Past her bodice.

9
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.780
Moments later, she's running for the town.

10
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.580
So why does a morning
walk turn into an escape?

11
00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.220
In this mission, you'll
meet Emily Dickinson,

12
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:32.910
whose poem was first printed in
1891, under a different title.

13
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.570
You'll hear its rhythm,
borrowed from hymns:

14
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.740
four beats, then three.

15
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.690
And you'll follow the
tide, stage by stage,

16
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.860
up the beach.

17
00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.180
Your mission: explain
why she ends up running.
